---
import LegalLayout from '../layouts/LegalLayout.astro';
import { SITE } from '../lib/site';

const breadcrumbs = [{ label: 'Home', href: '/' }, { label: 'Terms' }];
---

<LegalLayout
  title="Terms of use"
  description="The rules for using this independent study-resource site."
  breadcrumbs={breadcrumbs}
  updated="16 November 2026"
>
  <p>
    By using this site, you agree to these terms. If you do not agree, please do not use
    the site. These terms are a practical site policy, not legal advice.
  </p>

  <h2>Educational purpose</h2>
  <p>
    The site provides study material for educational use. It does not provide official
    university services, result checking, admission decisions, or legal advice. Always
    confirm syllabus, scheme, dates, eligibility, and results with the official AKTU
    source.
  </p>

  <h2>No warranty</h2>
  <p>
    We work to keep content accurate, but the site is provided "as is" without warranties
    of accuracy, completeness, fitness for a particular purpose, or uninterrupted
    availability. Subject codes, schemes, and exam patterns can change. Use the official
    documents as the final authority.
  </p>

  <h2>Permitted use</h2>
  <p>
    You may read, download, and print resources for your own study. You may share links to
    the site. You may not scrape the site at scale, bypass access controls, re-upload our
    PDFs as your own, remove attribution, or use the content to train or populate a
    competing commercial library without written permission.
  </p>

  <h2>Intellectual property</h2>
  <p>
    Original notes, solutions, question banks, diagrams, and site design are owned by
    their respective creators and are published under the licence recorded on each
    resource. Official AKTU documents remain the property of their owners. Open-licence
    material remains under its original licence and attribution requirements.
  </p>

  <h2>User submissions</h2>
  <p>
    If you submit a correction or resource, you confirm that you created it or have
    written permission to share it, and you grant us a non-exclusive, royalty-free licence
    to host, display, adapt, and distribute it with credit. We may remove any submission
    after a valid complaint.
  </p>

  <h2>Third-party links</h2>
  <p>
    The site links to official university pages and other third-party sites. We do not
    control those sites and are not responsible for their content, availability, or
    privacy practices.
  </p>

  <h2>Advertising</h2>
  <p>
    If ads are enabled, they will be clearly separated from download links. We will not
    use fake download buttons, countdowns, or interstitials. Ad providers may have their
    own terms and privacy policies.
  </p>

  <h2>Limitation of liability</h2>
  <p>
    To the extent permitted by law, we are not liable for any loss arising from reliance
    on the site, including academic outcomes, missed deadlines, or decisions made using an
    outdated document. Your use of the site is at your own risk.
  </p>

  <h2>Changes</h2>
  <p>
    We may update these terms as the site changes. The updated date at the bottom of this
    page shows the latest revision. Continued use after a change means you accept the
    revised terms.
  </p>

  <h2>Governing law</h2>
  <p>
    These terms are governed by the laws of India. Disputes are subject to the
    jurisdiction of the courts at the site operator's registered location, unless
    applicable law requires otherwise.
  </p>

  <h2>Contact</h2>
  <p>
    Questions: <a href={`mailto:${SITE.email}`}>{SITE.email}</a>
  </p>
  <p class="text-sm text-stone-500">
    TODO: have an Indian lawyer review these terms before commercial launch.
  </p>
</LegalLayout>
